{
  "id": "chapter-07",
  "number": 7,
  "title": "Objects",
  "summary": "Group related values together under one name.",
  "kicker": "Chapter 7",
  "heading": "Objects",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-object",
      "title": "What is an object?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An object groups related values together as named pairs. Instead of three loose variables for a user, you keep them in one tidy bundle. Each name is called a <strong>property</strong>."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "label": "Object",
          "code": "const user = {\n  name: \"Asha\",\n  age: 20,\n  isActive: true\n};"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/objects.png",
          "alt": "Handwritten note explaining objects",
          "caption": "Objects at a glance",
          "maxWidth": 720
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://javascript.info/object",
          "label": "More on javascript.info"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "using-properties",
      "title": "Reading and changing properties",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use a dot to read a property or to change it."
        },
        {
          "type": "compare",
          "cards": [
            {
              "title": "Read",
              "code": "user.name; // \"Asha\""
            },
            {
              "title": "Change",
              "code": "user.age = 21;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "run",
          "rows": 9,
          "code": "<p id=\"out\"></p>\n\n<script>\n  const user = { name: \"Asha\", age: 20 };\n  user.age = 21;\n  document.getElementById(\"out\").textContent =\n    user.name + \" is now \" + user.age;\n</script>"
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "An Angular component keeps its data as properties just like this — and your template reads them with <code>{{ user.name }}</code>."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "objects-recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "An object bundles related values under one name.",
            "Each value is a property, written as <code>name: value</code>.",
            "Read or change a property with a dot: <code>user.age</code>.",
            "Angular components hold their data the same way."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "group": "JavaScript"
}
